# charter-drift acknowledgement allowlist (T-2680)
#
# One `<tool_name>  # <reason>` per line. `#`-comment and blank lines are skipped.
# A tool listed here is STILL classified off-charter — it is simply acknowledged,
# so the daily canary does not alarm on it. Removing a line re-fires it.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# T-2483 shipped the charter-drift canary with a single detector: a six-family
# NAME regex (reactions / emoji / stars / pins / typing / polls) — the exact
# families P4 had just deleted. It reported `{checked:214, live_off_charter:0}`,
# which reads as a full-surface charter-traceability clean bill. It was not one:
# the regex could not see 28 live tools sitting in categories the binary itself
# names as analytics. `termlink_agent_top_repliers` is the same class of surface
# as the deprecated `termlink_agent_top_reacted`; only one of them is a word the
# regex knows.
#
# T-2680 added a CATEGORY detector, which makes those 28 visible. But whether
# they should be REMOVED is not the canary's call — that is an open, human-owned
# decision (T-2548, `started-work`, `owner: human`). Firing daily on a decision
# the human has not made yet is alarm fatigue; staying silent about them is the
# false assurance T-2680 exists to end.
#
# This file is the third option: the surface is acknowledged, counted, and
# reported (`acknowledged_count` in the JSON envelope, and a line in the healthy
# text output). The pending decision is VISIBLE rather than invisible, and any
# NEW off-charter tool fires immediately because it will not be listed here.
#
# THIS FILE IS GIT-TRACKED ON PURPOSE. The four sibling static checks keep their
# allowlists under `.context/working/`, which is gitignored — so their
# acknowledgements (and the cited reasons that justify them) do not survive a
# fresh clone, and the checks fire on every acknowledged site there. See T-2681.
#
# ON RESOLUTION OF T-2548
# -----------------------
# If the human decides to SUBTRACT: deprecate the tools, and delete their lines
# here — a deprecated tool is not live, so it no longer classifies as drift.
# If the human decides to KEEP: replace the T-2548 reason on each line with the
# charter verb it traces to, or adjust the category set in the canary.
# Either way this file should end up empty or re-justified — it is a ledger of
# an open question, not a permanent exemption.

